Rejected at Step 0 and documented in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1601.03361/REJECTED.md).

The native measurable-coloring problem lacks a bounded, exactly executable witness: the proof relies on conull/comeager sets, Borel uniformization, and infinite spanning-forest constructions. The finite planted-coloring fallback passes G and V but fails H:

- Track A fails because Brooks coloring has an `O(n+m)` constructive algorithm.
- Track B fails because, at fixed degree and the 256-element answer limit, both mechanical coloring and merely writing the witness require linear work with no meaningful compression gap.
- A finite adjacency-list surrogate would also discard the paper’s essential measurable/Borel structure.

These conclusions follow from the [full source paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.03361) and the known [linear-time constructive Brooks algorithm](https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.8023). Per Step 0, no generator, fabricated gate report, or oracle transcript was produced.
